<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jadeja</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Jadeja Rajputs</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jadeja are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> clan who ruled Kutch from the 16th century and spread into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Saurashtra</a>. In 1540 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jam-rawal">Jam Rawal</a> founded Nawanagar, and other branches held Rajkot, Gondal, Morvi, Malia, Kotda Sangani and many smaller states. The Jadeja <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> lasted until they acceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1947–1948.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jadeja.jpg" alt="Jadeja" width="320" height="490" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mrs Postan 1838 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jadeja_Chief.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
